# The Pi build this executor depends on.
#
# temporalio/pi branch moe/turn-steps, which stacks on PR #3, which stacks on PR #2:
#   #2 adds recordPrompt, prepareStep, step and resumeInterruptedTurn on AgentSession, which the
#      worker needs to drive a session one step at a time.
#   #3 adds pi.registerTurnExecutor, which the extension needs to make a session's own turns
#      durable.
#   moe/turn-steps adds modelCall, runToolCall and sealStep, which split a step so each tool call
#      is its own unit of work, and hands the same three to an executor as turn.steps.
# None of it is in the published @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent, so the dependency is a build of
# the fork.
#
# Bump PI_FORK_REF when the PR moves, then re-run scripts/setup-fork.sh.

PI_FORK_REPO=https://github.com/temporalio/pi.git
PI_FORK_REF=cd67f17a1cacdc25539f5b953ff12749f77028e0
